   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing the county of Rockland\nto impose an additional rate of sales and compensating use taxes",
    "basePrintNo": "S6029",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6029-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1210 & 1262-l, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6029\n\nSPONSOR: WEBER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to authorizing the county of\nRockland to impose an additional rate of sales and compensating use\ntaxes\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nRelates to extending the authorization for Rockland County to impose\nadditional rates of sales and compensating use taxes.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Clause 23 of subparagraph (i) of the opening paragraph of\nsection 1210 of the tax law, as amended by section 1 of item MM of\nsubpart C of part XXX of chapter 58 of the laws of 2020, is amended.\n\nSection 2: Section 1262-1 of the tax law, as amended by section 2 of\nitem MM 18 of subpart C of part XXX of chapter 58 of the laws of 2020,\nis amended.\n\nSection 3: Provides for an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Rockland County Legislature has requested legislation be introduced\nin the State Legislature to grant Rockland County the ability to extend\nthe additional rate of sales and compensating use taxes through November\n30, 2025.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
